<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Berea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1852</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Berea was fought on 20 December 1852 on the Berea plateau in present-day Lesotho between British forces under Sir George Cathcart and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sotho-people">Basotho</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moshoeshoe-i">Moshoeshoe I</a>. Cathcart's punitive expedition to seize <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> met stiff resistance, and the fighting was indecisive. Moshoeshoe then sent a conciliatory letter, allowing Cathcart to withdraw and claim success.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-berea.jpg" alt="Battle of Berea" width="320" height="547" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Enclosed in a dispatch from Governor Cathcart to the Secretary of State for the Colonies. Author name at bottom right... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_berea_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
